'' A LINK LINE PAST WINDOWS' 32,767-CHARACTER LIMIT GOES THROUGH A RESPONSE FILE (tiko-build
'' B0, 2026-10-11). It went on the command line, CreateProcess refused it, and the link
'' failed as TKO0116 'exit -1' -- 126 objects at absolute paths were enough. The root's
'' '#libpath's make a 36,000-character line here; it links, and the program runs. (A Linux
'' host has no such limit and keeps the line; '-v' says when a response file is used.)
'' TEST: cli
'' ENV: TIKO_LIBPATH=build/obj/rtlib/windows-x86_64
'' CLEAN: build/.lrf
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 tests/driver/src/long-link-line.bas -o build/.lrf/long.exe
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0116
'' RUN: build/.lrf/long.exe
'' EXPECT-RUN-OUT: linked
